2026-09-27T09:10:28.9273704Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9274095Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9274639Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9274900Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9275032Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9275301Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9275420Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9275598Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9275982Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9276217Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9276334Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9276627Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9277252Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9277477Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9277921Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9278311Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9278906Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9279287Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9279431Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9279838Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9280314Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9280600Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9280848Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9281187Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9281322Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9281553Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9281674Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9282613Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9283588Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9283776Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9284223Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9285231Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9285772Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9286254Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9287369Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9287839Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9287995Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9288309Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9288486Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9289263Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9290120Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9290634Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9291356Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:28.9291544Z 
